{
  "requirement": "Overrides the SDK’s OpenAI model, endpoint, credentials, or inference options. Omitted settings use the defaults in the agent configuration contract.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct OpenAiConfig {\n    pub model: Option<String>,\n    pub endpoint: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key_env: Option<String>,\n    pub api_key: Option<SecretString>,\n    pub options: BTreeMap<String, OptionValue>,\n}\n\nimpl OpenAiConfig {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n    pub fn model(self, model: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn endpoint(self, endpoint: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key_env(self, api_key_env: String) -> Self;\n    pub fn api_key(self, api_key: SecretString) -> Self;\n    pub fn option(self, key: String, value: OptionValue) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Debug for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Default for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl PartialEq for OpenAiConfig;\nimpl Serialize for OpenAiConfig;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.OpenAiConfig`. The covered obligations are the struct shape, the builders, the omitted-setting defaults and the trait implementations.\n\n**Shape and builders**\n- `backend_builders_set_only_the_requested_fields` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs` checks that `OpenAiConfig::new()` serializes to `{}`.\n- The same test applies `model`, `endpoint`, `api_key_env`, `api_key` and `option` and checks that the serialized result has exactly those fields.\n- That test also repeats `option(\"a\", …)` and shows the second value replaces the first while `b` is kept.\n- `all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials` round-trips a full OpenAI configuration through serde, including nested options.\n\n**Defaults for omitted settings**\n- `option_defaults_and_credential_resolution_are_deterministic` checks that `OpenAiConfig::default()` resolves the model to `gpt-6.1-sol` and the endpoint to `https://api.openai.com/v1`.\n- It also checks the default options `max_output_tokens` = 16384 and `reasoning.effort` = `low`.\n- It checks that a custom `api_key_env` is the variable consulted, because the error names it.\n- It checks that an explicit `api_key` is used.\n- `openai_uses_the_default_credential_variable` runs a child process with `OPENAI_API_KEY` set and asserts that `OpenAiConfig::new().resolved_api_key()` returns that value.\n- `openai_inference_options_only_fill_missing_defaults` checks that `{\"backend\":\"openai\"}` equals `OpenAiConfig::new()`.\n- That test also checks the default options for a minimal configuration, a user-supplied `max_output_tokens`, a `reasoning` object that adds `summary`, and a user-supplied `reasoning.effort`.\n- `supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport` in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` supplies the `local-test` model and an endpoint and checks that requests use them. It also checks that the default `max_output_tokens` of 16384 is sent.\n\n**Trait implementations**\n- `Serialize`, `Deserialize` and `PartialEq` are asserted directly in the tests above.\n- `Default` is exercised through `OpenAiConfig::default()`.\n- `Clone` and `Debug` are plain `#[derive]`s, so they have no conditional or transformation of their own to test. `AgentConfig` derives both, so they are compile-checked.\n- `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` covers the public export.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "1e27ef26f764835e7d12b55c94dc204c3b3fe9b16be8fc68565e50322e5ce3e9",
